      "text": "Both profiles carry two counterparty disputes in the trailing 90 days — rider_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d = 2 on EV-RPROF-09110 and driver_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d = 2 on EV-DPROF-09110 — and the rider's own filing states this is 'another dispute with the same driver'. Read together they show two or more no-show disputes between the same rider and driver in the trailing 90 days, which is a mandatory escalation trigger under POL-NS-09(c). These are precisely the two fields POL-GEN-01 makes citable for this test, so the point rests on the named counters and not on any reputation or lifetime counter such as prior_no_show_flags.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-09110", "EV-DPROF-09110"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The escalation the rider seeks is terminal and it is the outcome that protects the rider on this record. Under POL-NS-09 no monetary ruling issues and the disputed fee is placed on hold rather than collected or refunded, and POL-GEN-03 confirms ESCALATE always replaces the monetary ruling. The fare record as it stands shows the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee with payment_status 'PENDING' and refund_issued_sgd 0.00, so escalation leaves the rider not carrying the contested charge while a human reviewer settles the pattern question between these two parties.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-09110", "EV-TRIP-09110"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "An honest concession, so that no argument is made on it: POL-NS-04 cannot carry this case. The driver answered the rider's 06:51:40 chat message at 06:52:00, twenty seconds later and well inside the 120-second window, so limb (b) fails on the chat log; and the rider's own device fixes sit 519 m from the pickup pin with a rider_qualifying_fix_count of 0 against the 100 m STANDARD presence radius, so limb (c) fails affirmatively on admissible fixes. Rider-side relief therefore cannot come from POL-NS-04 and must come from escalation under POL-NS-09.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-09110", "EV-GPS-09110"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.rider_qualifying_fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Disclosure: EV-ADVIS-09110-01 is MISSING — status MISSING, weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, because no traffic advisory matched this pickup road and waiting window — and its absence is itself citable. The consequence is that nothing in the record corroborates the kerbside conditions on this pickup road and the POL-NS-06(i) accumulation limb is unavailable, and any attempt to rely on limb (i) against a MISSING artifact engages POL-NS-09 rather than exonerating anyone. The entire charge therefore rests on a single in-geofence run of 330 seconds that cleared the 300-second STANDARD minimum by only 30 seconds — one further reason this case belongs with a human reviewer rather than an automated collection.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-09110-01", "EV-GPS-09110"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06", "POL-NS-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.accumulated_dwell.shortfall_sec"
    }
  ]
}

