    "confidence": 0.85,
    "explanation": "To both parties: this case goes to a human reviewer and the disputed SGD 4.00 cancellation fee is placed on hold — neither collected from the rider nor refunded to her — while review is pending.\n\nWhy escalation is mandatory. POL-NS-09(c) requires escalation where rider_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d and driver_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d together show two or more no-show disputes between the same rider and driver in the trailing 90 days. EV-RPROF-09110 records 2 and EV-DPROF-09110 records 2, and the rider's own filing describes this as 'another dispute with the same driver'. Those are the exact two fields POL-GEN-01 makes citable for this test; the lifetime counters prior_no_show_flags (rider 1, driver 2) are context only and are not used to build the finding. The open question the reviewer must settle is whether this repeated pair-level dispute pattern changes what should happen to this charge.\n\nThe merits, for the reviewer. The driver met every element of POL-NS-01: EV-TRIP-09110 carries an 'arrived' event at 06:50:20 and a driver termination at 06:55:30 with reason RIDER_NO_SHOW; EV-GPS-09110 places the driver inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius throughout — all 34 fixes sit about 24 m from the pin — with a continuous qualifying in-geofence hold of 330 seconds measured from the first qualifying fix at 06:50:00, 30 seconds above the 300-second STANDARD minimum (shortfall_sec -30.0), and no boarding event is recorded. POL-NS-02 is satisfied; POL-NS-05 is not engaged (the driver was stationary at 0.0 km/h, 24 m from the pin, so the arrival marker is true); POL-NS-06 shows no shortfall to refund; POL-NS-03 does not apply because the driver was inside the arrival radius, not stationary outside it within 400 m (registered_pickup_points is 1). POL-NS-04 does not assist the rider: the driver answered her 06:51:40 message at 06:52:00, 20 seconds later and inside the 120-second window, so limb (b) fails, and her device fixes sit about 519 m from the pin with 0 qualifying fixes, so limb (c) fails affirmatively. But for the escalation, POL-NS-07 would pay the driver 80% of the SGD 4.00 fee, i.e. SGD 3.20; the anti-farming check does not trip (no_show_terminations_30d = 1, below 4, and 1 / 120 = 0.008, below 0.08), so nothing is withheld on that ground. Because POL-NS-09(c) is mandatory and terminal, no monetary ruling issues today and no compensation is paid now.\n\nEvidence integrity. The SGD 4.00 cancellation-fee line equals the greater of the STANDARD zone-class fee (SGD 4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00), so there is no POL-NS-08(d) fare defect. The trace has 100% coverage, no gaps and 34 fixes, and the chat log holds the 4 messages the trip record reports, so nothing is impaired under POL-NS-08(a)-(d). EV-ADVIS-09110-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT): it can carry no fact, but nothing turns on it here, because the dwell already exceeds the minimum and there is no shortfall for POL-NS-06(i) accumulation to manufacture.\n\nNo referral issues: none of the clauses that produce a referral (POL-RD-06(c), POL-RD-09(4), POL-NS-05(ii), POL-NS-07's anti-farming packet instruction) fires on this record, so referrals is empty."
  },
